			<h1>Auld Lang Syne (L'hora dels adéus)</h1>

			<p>
				<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auld_Lang_Syne">Auld Lang Syne</a
				> is a traditional Scottish song that is often played at the end of events
				(<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ceilidh" target="_blank"
					>ceilidhs</a
				> in particular). It is also a song in Catalan, known as L'hora dels adéus.
				In both languages it is a solemn and rousing song of farewells and times
				gone by.
			</p>

			<p>
				In many countries it is also sang at midnight at the start of the year,
				the 1st of January.
			</p>

			<p>
				If you are playing at a ceilidh, you may wish to play it twice slow, and
				then play the B part twice fast.
			</p>

